   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "On Linux, a file's modification time comes from a coarse kernel clock that can run a few milliseconds behind the wall clock. A report written just after the run starts can therefore look older than the start time and be rejected as stale. This mostly hits the new fast unit tests on Linux CI, which then fail and block the change from landing; a real bun test run starts far too slowly to fall inside that window.",
   "reproduction": {
